{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:10.1074/jbc.M113.545822","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":5,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"24550394","source":"MED","pmid":"24550394","pmcid":"PMC3975039","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC3975039"]},"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m113.545822","title":"Interleukin-6 (IL-6) trans signaling drives a STAT3-dependent pathway that leads to hyperactive transforming growth factor-β (TGF-β) signaling promoting SMAD3 activation and fibrosis via Gremlin protein.","authorString":"O'Reilly S, O'Reilly S, Ciechomska M, Cant R, van Laar JM.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"O'Reilly S","lastName":"O'Reilly","firstName":"Steven","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7483-740X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"From the Musculoskeletal Research Group, Institute of Cellular Medicine, 4th Floor Cookson Building, Framlington Place, Newcastle upon Tyne NE2 4HH, United Kingdom."}]}},{"fullName":"O'Reilly S","lastName":"O'Reilly","firstName":"Steven","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3416-7330"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"From the Musculoskeletal Research Group, Institute of Cellular Medicine, 4th Floor Cookson Building, Framlington Place, Newcastle upon Tyne NE2 4HH, United Kingdom."}]}},{"fullName":"Ciechomska M","lastName":"Ciechomska","firstName":"Marzena","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0961-6130"}},{"fullName":"Cant R","lastName":"Cant","firstName":"Rachel","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"van Laar JM","lastName":"van Laar","firstName":"Jacob M","initials":"JM"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7483-740X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0961-6130"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3416-7330"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"14","volume":"289","journalIssueId":2146745,"dateOfPublication":"2014 Apr","monthOfPublication":4,"yearOfPublication":2014,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Biol Chem","title":"The Journal of biological chemistry","essn":"1083-351X","issn":"0021-9258","isoabbreviation":"J Biol Chem","nlmid":"2985121R"},"printPublicationDate":"2014-04-01"},"pubYear":"2014","pageInfo":"9952-9960","abstractText":"Fibrosis is a common and intractable condition associated with various pathologies. It is characterized by accumulation of an excessive amount of extracellular matrix molecules that primarily include collagen type I. IL-6 is a profibrotic cytokine that is elevated in the prototypic fibrotic autoimmune condition systemic sclerosis and is known to induce collagen I expression, but the mechanism(s) behind this induction are currently unknown. Using healthy dermal fibroblasts in vitro, we analyzed the signaling pathways that underscore the IL-6-mediated induction of collagen. We show that IL-6 trans signaling is important and that the effect is dependent on STAT3; however, the effect is indirect and mediated through enhanced TGF-β signaling and the classic downstream cellular mediator Smad3. This is due to induction of the bone morphogenetic protein (BMP) antagonist Gremlin-1, and we show that Gremlin-1 is profibrotic and is mediated through canonical TGF-β signaling.","affiliation":"From the Musculoskeletal Research Group, Institute of Cellular Medicine, 4th Floor Cookson Building, Framlington Place, Newcastle upon Tyne NE2 4HH, United Kingdom.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Clinical Trial","research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cells, Cultured"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Fibroblasts","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Fibrosis","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"PA","qualifierName":"pathology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Collagen Type I","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"BI","qualifierName":"biosynthesis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Intercellular Signaling Peptides and Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Transforming Growth Factor beta","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Bone Morphogenetic Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"BI","qualifierName":"biosynthesis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Interleukin-6","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Signal Transduction"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Female"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"STAT3 Transcription Factor","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName